{"name":"Bedside Manner","hex":"#adb7c1","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bedside manner","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The ability of a doctor, medic, nurse, or other healthcare professional, to interact with their patients; the quality or nature of their interactive style. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bedside_manner"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bedside Manner (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Bedside Manner is a 1945 American comedy film directed by Andrew L. Stone and starring John Carroll, Ruth Hussey, Charles Ruggles and Ann Rutherford. It is based on a 1944 Saturday Evening Post story of the same name by Robert Carson and was distributed by United Artists. The film was re-released in 1950 by Astor Pictures under the title Her Favorite Patient."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e9/Bedside_Manner_poster.jpg/330px-Bedside_Manner_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedside_Manner_(film)","wikidata":"Q4879432"},{"title":"Doctor–patient relationship","blocks":[{"text":"The doctor–patient relationship is a central part of health care and the practice of medicine. A doctor–patient relationship is formed when a doctor attends to a patient's medical needs and is usually through consent. This relationship is built on trust, respect, communication, and a common understanding of both the doctor and patients' sides. The trust aspect of this relationship goes is mutual: the doctor trusts the patient to reveal any information that may be relevant to the case, and in turn, the patient trusts the doctor to respect their privacy and not disclose this information to outside parties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Doctor_explains_x-ray_to_patient.jpg/330px-Doctor_explains_x-ray_to_patient.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor%E2%80%93patient_relationship","wikidata":"Q905758"},{"title":"Bedside","blocks":[{"text":"Bedside is a 1934 American pre-Code drama film starring Warren William, Jean Muir and Allen Jenkins."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/37/Bedside_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedside","wikidata":"Q45281386"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e9/Bedside_Manner_poster.jpg/330px-Bedside_Manner_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e9/Bedside_Manner_poster.jpg/330px-Bedside_Manner_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABedside_Manner_poster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Doctor_explains_x-ray_to_patient.jpg/500px-Doctor_explains_x-ray_to_patient.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Doctor_explains_x-ray_to_patient.jpg/1280px-Doctor_explains_x-ray_to_patient.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Doctor_explains_x-ray_to_patient.jpg/500px-Doctor_explains_x-ray_to_patient.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A medical practitioner explains an x-ray to the patient.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADoctor_explains_x-ray_to_patient.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Doctor_advises_patient.jpg/500px-Doctor_advises_patient.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/